      "good": "import ZestButton from \u0027jattac.libs.web.zest-button\u0027;\nimport ZestTextbox from \u0027jattac.libs.web.zest-textbox\u0027;\n\nexport const Form = () =\u003E (\n  \u003Cdiv\u003E\n    \u003CZestTextbox label=\u0022Name\u0022 /\u003E\n    \u003CZestButton\u003ESave\u003C/ZestButton\u003E\n  \u003C/div\u003E\n);",
      "bad": "export const Form = () =\u003E (\n  \u003Cdiv\u003E\n    \u003Cinput type=\u0022text\u0022 /\u003E\n    \u003Cbutton onClick={save}\u003ESave\u003C/button\u003E\n    \u003Ctable\u003E\u003Ctbody /\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\n  \u003C/div\u003E\n);",
      "notes": "Whether a given custom-built component duplicates one of the listed libraries (layout, sidekick menu, overflow menu, tabs wrappers, hand-rolled menus), and whether timer-based polling (setInterval/setTimeout loops, repeated fetch) should use jattac-web-poller. Checkbox, radio and select elements are not covered. Whether the packages are installed is already visible in front-end/package.json. A reviewer should judge these.",
